/*
 * Tree files support.
 *
 * An export using treefiles is stored as a tree of small files
 * rather than as one large file. The exported device is divided
 * into blocks of TREEPAGESIZE bytes, and each block is stored in
 * its own file. The block files are spread over a tree of
 * directories with at most TREEDIRSIZE entries per directory, so
 * that neither the files nor the directories grow very large.
 * This is useful on filesystems that do not handle large files
 * well, such as fuse/ftpfs or davfs.
 *
 * A block that has never been written reads as all zeroes; such
 * blocks do not have a file at all. When a block is trimmed
 * away, its file is deleted again.
 */

